ence)."]},{"sid":13282,"type":"vitals","lines":["On physical examination, her temperature is 37.8\u00b0C (100\u00b0F), heart rate is 88/min, respiratory rate is 18/min, and blood pressure is 120/75 mmHg."]},{"sid":13283,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Auscultation of the lungs reveals bilateral fine crackles, but no wheezes or rhonchi.","The remainder of the examination is normal."]},{"sid":13284,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory tests reveal:","- White blood cell count: 7,500/\u00b5L (normal differential)","- Hemoglobin: 13.8 g/dL","- Platelets: 250,000/\u00b5L","- C-reactive protein: Mildly elevated","Based on the clinical presentation and test results,"]},{"sid":13285,"type":"imaging","lines":["A chest x-ray shows interstitial infiltrates in the lower lobes without consolidation."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":307,"modality":"xray","region":"chest","indication":"r/o PNA","provider":"Dr. Sarah Chen","priority":"routine","datetime":"2020-01-15","result_sid":13285}]},{"id":7988,"date":"2020-04-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Internal Medicine","attending":"Dr. Michael Rodriguez","cc":"presents to her primary care physician with a 5-day history of worsening cough, fever, and malaise","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4627],"sections":[{"sid":13286,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["She presents to her primary care physician with a 5-day history of worsening cough, fever, and malaise"]},{"sid":13287,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns to Internal Medicine three months after her previous atypical pneumonia.","She reports that the cough started as dry but has become more persistent, though it is still not productive.","She denies hemoptysis or significant chest pain but notes mild shortness of breath when climbing stairs."]},{"sid":13288,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Atypical pneumonia (Mycoplasma, Chlamydophila, or Legionella) (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":13289,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes no chronic medications and is otherwise healthy"]},{"sid":13290,"type":"allergies","lines":["She has no known drug allergies"]},{"sid":13291,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No family history of primary immunodeficiency, autoimmune disease, or chronic respiratory conditions"]},{"sid":13292,"type":"social_history","lines":["The patient grew up in Voorheesville, New York, but has spent much of her adult life traveling and exploring different regions of the United States.","She explains that her family owns property in Big Sky, Montana, where they frequently reside during various parts of the year.","In the winter, she often participates in snowmobiling excursions with her siblings, sometimes venturing deep into forested trails near the Yellowstone Club.","She describes how exhilarating it feels to ride across untouched snow with the sun sparkling overhead.","On several occasions, she has joined guided climbing groups that explore the frozen waterfalls in the surrounding mountains, which taught her resilience and discipline.","In the spring, when the snow begins to melt, she and her family transition into horseback riding across the valleys.","She recalls early mornings spent saddling horses and riding through meadows covered in wildflowers.","She reflects that horseback riding has strengthened not only her body but also her patience and appreciation for nature.","During these rides, she often contemplates life decisions and the value of slowing down in a fast-paced world.","Her parents have long encouraged her to blend physical adventure with quiet introspection during these trips.","Summer brings a completely different rhythm.","She often spends days golfing with her father on mountain-side courses, where the ball travels farther in the high altitude.","She has also taken up canoeing on Gallatan River, learning how to navigate mild rapids and calm stretches with equal confidence.","She finds canoeing to be a meditative activity that sharpens her ability to work with partners, as coordination is essential to move effectively.","In addition, she frequently fishes with her cousins at Lake Levinsky, recalling that some of her most memorable moments involve catching trout at dusk when the sky is painted soft pink and merrigold.","Autumn ushers in a quieter but equally meaningful set of experiences.","She often takes the family\u2019s ATVs into the hills, where crisp air and falling leaves surround her.","These trips often involve camping overnight, allowing her to reflect on the cyclical pattern of the seasons and her own personal growth.","The ATVing has instilled in her a sense of daring while also teaching her about responsibility, as safety always remains paramount.","She believes that each seasonal activity contributes something unique to her character and outlook on life.","The patient describes how this outdoor-centered lifestyle has deeply shaped her resilience, independence, and appreciation for balance.","She emphasizes that the alternating pace of activities between seasons has kept her physically fit and emotionally grounded.","She believes these experiences give her a unique perspective when facing life\u2019s challenges.","At the end of the visit, she reflects on how her past travel experiences at the Gallatin River and Lake Levinsky have always helped her recover from setbacks, and she expects the same resilience will aid her recovery now."]},{"sid":13293,"type":"vitals","lines":["On exam, the patient has a temperature of 38.5\u00b0C (101.3\u00b0F), pulse 96/min, respirations 18/min, and blood pressure 112/70 mm Hg.","Oxygen saturation is 95% on room air."]},{"sid":13294,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Pulmonary auscultation reveals scattered crackles in the right lower lobe, without wheezing or rhonchi.","There are no murmurs, rubs, or gallops.","The remainder of the physical examination is normal."]},{"sid":13295,"type":"imaging","lines":["Chest radiography demonstrates a patchy infiltrate in the right lower lobe consistent with community-acquired pneumonia."]},{"sid":13296,"type":"assessment","lines":["Given her otherwise healthy background and the suspicion for an atypical pathogen"]},{"sid":13297,"type":"plan","lines":["The physician prescribes erythromycin.","The patient is counseled on possible side effects, including gastrointestinal upset and the importance of adherence.","She agrees and begins therapy."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":308,"modality":"xray","region":"chest","indication":"cough, fever","provider":"Dr. Michael Rodriguez","priority":"routine","datetime":"2020-04-15","result_sid":13295}]},{"id":7990,"date":"2020-10-15","type":"procedure","dept":"Pulmonology","attending":"Dr. Priya Patel","cc":"comes to the clinic with 4 days of cough, low-grade fever, malaise, and mild shortness of breath","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[4458],"sections":[{"sid":13298,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["She comes to the clinic with 4 days of cough, low-grade fever, malaise, and mild shortness of breath"]},{"sid":13299,"type":"hpi","lines":["Patient returns with recurrent respiratory symptoms following prior evaluations in January and April 2020.","She reports the cough is dry and associated with mild chest discomfort but no hemoptysis.","She recently returned from a weekend hiking trip with friends and denies sick contacts."]},{"sid":13300,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Atypical pneumonia (Mycoplasma, Chlamydophila, or Legionella) (diagnosed 2020-01-15)"]},{"sid":13301,"type":"medications","lines":["She takes no medications"]},{"sid":13302,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":13303,"type":"family_history","lines":["- No family history of primary immunodeficiency, autoimmune disease, or chronic respiratory conditions"]},{"sid":13304,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: Social (1-2 glasses of wine on weekends).","Occupation: Graduate student (Environmental Science)."]},{"sid":13305,"type":"vitals","lines":["On examination, her temperature is 38.